XICYC l. 69 : - F1 (from [R15a]): Ω_t ⊴ Ω_(t+1) pointwise, for every step t. A Howard step switches exactly at the movers where the new successor is
XICYC l. 70 :   strictly better, so I is non-empty and unambiguous (one switch per vertex).
XICYC l. 71 : - F2 (from [VJ]): if Ω(v) ⊴ Ω′(v) and Λ ≠ Λ′, then the reward of Λ′ is strictly larger. Distinct vertices have distinct rewards.
XICYC l. 72 : - F3 (from [VJ], plays of a positional pair): let v be a vertex with Λ_t(v) ≠ v. Then Ω_t(v) = ext(v, Ω_t(nx_t(v))), where nx_t(v) is
XICYC l. 73 :   σ_t(v) for an Even v and σ̄_t(v) for an Odd v, and ext(v, (Λ, Π, k)) := (Λ, Π ∪ {v if v is more relevant than Λ}, k + 1).
XICYC l. 74 :   Also Ω_t(w) = (w, ∅, 0) when Λ_t(w) = w.
